11
00:48:07,500 --> 00:48:13,500
I Know Who Killed Me is a 2007 American psychological thriller film
directed by Chris Sivertson from a screenplay by Jeff Hammond.

12
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
It stars Lindsay Lohan as a young woman who is abducted
and tortured by a sadistic serial killer.

13
00:56:52,500 --> 00:56:58,500
After surviving the abduction, she insists that her
identity is that of another woman.

14
01:01:15,000 --> 01:01:21,000
Julia Ormond, Neal McDonough, Brian Geraghty, Garcelle Beauvais, Spencer
Garrett and Bonnie Aarons appear in supporting roles.

15
01:05:37,500 --> 01:05:43,500
The film received intense negative media coverage during production and upon its
release, as Lohan publicly struggled with addiction and other personal issues.

16
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Filming took place mostly in California, from December 2006 to March 2007.

17
01:14:22,500 --> 01:14:28,500
It was theatrically released in the United States by
TriStar Pictures on July 27, 2007.

18
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
It was promptly deemed a failure and called one of the worst films ever made, being the most
awarded at the 28th Golden Raspberry Awards, winning seven of eight nominations.

19
01:23:07,500 --> 01:23:13,500
The film did, however, attain a more successful home video
performance, having almost quadrupled its U.S.

20
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
box office gross in estimated domestic DVD sales.

21
01:31:52,500 --> 01:31:58,500
I Know Who Killed Me subsequently developed a cult following that has reexamined it as a modern giallo and
several screenings of it have been put together by historic theaters and film festivals.

22
01:36:15,000 --> 01:36:21,000
The film explores themes of daughter, sadism, kidnapping, sadistic, striptease.

23
01:40:37,500 --> 01:40:43,500
The tone is mind_bending and dark and intense.
